and thread.reply-count changed from '23 replies' to '24 replies' (+1).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-5\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"On thread-1 (authored by TechExplorer, another user): clicking thread.upvote raised thread.upvotes 47 -> 48 immediately and applied selected styling (bg-primary/10 text-primary); clicking again removed it, 48 -> 47 with selected styling cleared — confirming a single toggleable vote rather than repeated increments. Clicking thread.replies.item.reply-1.upvote raised reply upvotes 15 -> 16 with selected state true. All updates rendered immediately with no reload.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Search 'zebra' (lowercase) matched title 'QA Alpha Zebra Thread about testing' only -> case-insensitive title match. Search 'MENTIONS' (uppercase, word appears only in the body) returned the same single thread -> case-insensitive body match. Search 'qqzzxxnomatch123' returned 0 rows with clear feedback 'No threads found. Try adjusting your search terms.' and summary 'Showing results for \\\"qqzzxxnomatch123\\\"'.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"/category/tech listed only Technology threads (thread-7 'Building a mechanical keyboard', thread-1 'What programming language should I learn in 2024?', plus new thread-1787888348120). Switching to /category/gaming changed the result set to only thread-4 'Best indie games of 2023 that flew under the radar' (Gaming). Filtering is correct per category.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Most Active initial order by reply count: 89, 67, 45, 41, 38, 34(thread-5), 31(thread-3), 24, 0 — strictly descending. Added 4 replies to thread-3 (31 -> 35). Re-opening Most Active gave 89, 67, 45, 41, 38, 35(thread-3), 34(thread-5), 24, 0 — thread-3 correctly overtook thread-5, so the