    "content": "All 18 checklist items have been tested and recorded — **11 PASS, 7 FAIL**.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Working well:** The core forum loop is solid — registration with duplicate rejection, profile bio/interests editing, thread publishing into categories, live replies, single-toggle upvoting on threads and replies, case-insensitive keyword search across title and body, category filtering, author profile pages, and both Trending (by upvotes) and Most Active (by replies) sort orders that correctly re-rank when activity changes.\n\n**The 7 failures, roughly by severity:**\n\n1. **CS-17 — Authentication is effectively bypassed.** Signing in with a deliberately wrong password (`wrongpassword999`) still created a logged-in session. The password is never verified. This is a security defect, not just a UX gap.\n\n2. **FT-18 — Nothing persists.** A page reload resets the entire app to seed data: accounts, sessions, authored threads, replies and votes all vanish, and `localStorage` is empty. Note this contrasts with **FT-13**, which passed — state survives logout/login fine *within* one loaded page, so the state layer works; it simply is never written anywhere durable.\n\n3. **CS-22 — Blank dead-end page.** An unauthenticated user hitting `/new-thread` gets a completely empty page (no redirect, no sign-in form, no message), with no create-thread affordance anywhere while logged out. There is no path to authenticate and return.\n\n4. **CT-21 / CT-19 — Inflated placeholder counts.** Community stats (1,045 threads / 4,823 replies / 892 members) and per-category counts are hardcoded against only 9 real threads, and never update on creation. Relatedly, thread headers claim e.g. \"23 replies\" while only 2 replies actually render. Deltas are applied correctly (+1 on each new reply), so only the seeded baselines are fabricated.\n\n5. **CT-20 — No recent time window.** Trending and Most Active claim recent popularity but state no window and rank on all-time totals; two-year-old seeded threads top the list while content created today ranks last.\n\n6. **CS-14 — Silent validation.** Empty and whitespace-only submissions are correctly blocked, but no message ever identifies which field is missing.\n\nOne methodology note worth flagging: I verified FT-13 before FT-18 by design, since a reload destroys all state. The FT-18 evidence was captured from a reload that had already occurred, and I rebuilt a fresh account and content set afterward to test FT-13 cleanly in a single uninterrupted page load."
